---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of Use — Crystal Lattice"
  description="Crystal Lattice terms of use. Open source software distributed under the Apache 2.0 license."
>
  <Nav />
  <main class="prose-page">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="header">
        <p class="label">Legal</p>
        <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
        <p class="meta">Effective date: May 2025</p>
      </div>

      <div class="content">
        <section>
          <h2>Open source software</h2>
          <p>
            Crystal Lattice — including the CLI, server, agent-core SDK, bridge service,
            and mobile app — is open source software distributed under the
            <a href="https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Apache License, Version 2.0</a>.
          </p>
          <p>
            You may use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and sell copies
            of the software in accordance with the terms of that license. A copy of the license
            is included in the source repository and is also available at the link above.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Website terms</h2>
          <p>
            These terms govern your use of crystallattice.dev (the "Site"). By accessing the
            Site, you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, please do not use the Site.
          </p>
          <p>
            The Site provides information about the Crystal Lattice open source project.
            Content is provided for informational purposes only.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>No warranty</h2>
          <p>
            The software is provided "as is," without warranty of any kind, express or implied,
            including but not limited to the warranties of merchantability, fitness for a
            particular purpose, and non-infringement.
          </p>
          <p>
            In no event shall the authors or copyright holders be liable for any claim, damages,
            or other liability, whether in an action of contract, tort or otherwise, arising from,
            out of, or in connection with the software or the use or other dealings in the software.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Your responsibilities</h2>
          <p>When using Crystal Lattice, you are responsible for:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Complying with the terms of service of any AI provider you connect to (OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, OpenRouter, etc.).</li>
            <li>Securing your server appropriately if you expose it on a network. The server binds to <code>0.0.0.0</code> when you pass <code>--host 0.0.0.0</code> — only do this on trusted networks or behind appropriate access controls.</li>
            <li>Managing and protecting any API keys used to configure AI providers.</li>
            <li>Ensuring your use of AI-generated content complies with applicable laws in your jurisdiction.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Third-party services</h2>
          <p>
            Crystal Lattice integrates with third-party AI providers. Use of those services is
            governed by their respective terms of service and privacy policies, not by these terms.
            We are not affiliated with, endorsed by, or responsible for any third-party provider.
          </p>
          <p>
            The bridge service is an optional component. Use of the bridge service is subject to
            its own infrastructure terms where applicable.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
          <p>
            The Crystal Lattice name, logo, and associated branding are the property of the
            project maintainers. The Apache 2.0 license grants broad rights to use, modify,
            and distribute the software itself, but does not grant rights to use the project's
            trademarks or branding in ways that imply official endorsement.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Contributions</h2>
          <p>
            Contributions to the Crystal Lattice project are governed by the Apache 2.0 license
            and the contribution guidelines in the repository. By submitting a pull request,
            you agree that your contribution may be distributed under those terms.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Changes</h2>
          <p>
            We may update these terms as the project evolves. Changes will be posted to this
            page with an updated effective date. Continued use of the Site after changes
            constitutes acceptance of the updated terms.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Contact</h2>
          <p>
            Questions about these terms can be directed to the project via GitHub Issues
            or the contact information in the repository.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .prose-page {
    padding: 5rem 0 6rem;
  }

  .container {
    max-width: 680px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 1.5rem;
  }

  .header {
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
    padding-bottom: 2rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .label {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent-soft);
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .meta {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--text-5);
  }

  .content {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2.5rem;
  }

  section h2 {
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text-2);
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }

  section p {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--text-4);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  section p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  section a {
    color: var(--accent-soft);
    transition: color 0.15s;
  }

  section a:hover {
    color: var(--accent-pale);
  }

  section ul {
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.625rem;
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }

  section ul li {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--text-4);
    line-height: 1.65;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    position: relative;
  }

  section ul li::before {
    content: "—";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--border-strong);
  }

  code {
    font-size: 0.875em;
  }
</style>
